/P 120 0 R
/T (CONCLUSION  We successfully deployed ahybrid computingarchitecturecombining HPC and Spark. MPI was lightweight and faster to set up for smaller tasks. Spark offered better scalability and fault-tolerance. Both methods were effective at handling bioinformatics ML tasks. We gained real-world experience in systems setup, distributed ML, and debugging parallel computing environments.)
/E (CONCLUSION  We successfully deployed ahybrid computingarchitecturecombining HPC and Spark. MPI was lightweight and faster to set up for smaller tasks. Spark offered better scalability and fault-tolerance. Both methods were effective at handling bioinformatics ML tasks. We gained real-world experience in systems setup, distributed ML, and debugging parallel computing environments.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
